From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 01:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] net: stmmac: dwmac-sun8i: RX threshold mode for frames near
 the RX FIFO size

In store-and-forward mode the RX DMA starts only when the whole frame is
in the 16 KiB RX FIFO. A 16372-byte frame leaves 12 bytes for the next
frame arriving back to back, and the RX FIFO overflows whenever the DMA
does not drain at once (TCP at that size: 53 of 76321 frames lost;
9018-byte frames: none).

Receive in threshold mode (RX_TH 64, the reset value) when the largest
frame of the MTU leaves less than 4 KiB of the RX FIFO free.
stmmac_dma_conf gains max_frame for this.

Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-sun8i.c | 8 ++++++++
 drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac.h      | 2 ++
 drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c | 1 +
 3 files changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-sun8i.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-sun8i.c
index 6a438dd..c7dab99 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-sun8i.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-sun8i.c
@@ -585,6 +585,14 @@ static void sun8i_dwmac_dma_operation_mode_rx(struct stmmac_priv *priv,
 {
 	u32 v;
 
+	/* In store-and-forward mode the RX DMA starts once the whole frame
+	 * is in the FIFO. With less than 4 KiB left, a frame arriving back to
+	 * back overflows the FIFO unless the DMA drains it at once: receive
+	 * frames that large in threshold mode (RX_TH 64, the reset value).
+	 */
+	if (mode == SF_DMA_MODE && priv->dma_conf.max_frame > fifosz - 4096)
+		mode = 64;
+
 	v = readl(ioaddr + EMAC_RX_CTL1);
 	if (mode == SF_DMA_MODE) {
 		v |= EMAC_RX_MD;
diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac.h b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac.h
index d2d387f..8ad6b57 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac.h
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac.h
@@ -217,6 +217,8 @@ struct stmmac_rfs_entry {
 
 struct stmmac_dma_conf {
 	unsigned int dma_buf_sz;
+	/* largest frame of the MTU, with two VLAN tags and the FCS */
+	unsigned int max_frame;
 
 	/* RX Queue */
 	struct stmmac_rx_queue rx_queue[MTL_MAX_RX_QUEUES];
diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c
index a385d5e..68e01bf 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c
@@ -4079,6 +4079,7 @@ stmmac_setup_dma_desc(struct stmmac_priv *priv, unsigned int mtu)
 	}
 
 	len = mtu + ETH_HLEN + 2 * VLAN_HLEN + ETH_FCS_LEN;
+	dma_conf->max_frame = len;
 
 	/* Returns 0 or BUF_SIZE_16KiB if len > 8KiB and dwmac4 or ring mode */
 	bfsize = stmmac_set_16kib_bfsize(priv, len);
